## Store map audit — H-E-B 229

I reran everything and treated the committed artifacts as untrusted. All five passes complete.

### Pass 1 — Mechanical: PASS
`./rebuild.sh 229` → exit 0, 780 tests pass. `report.json`: `"verify": []`, both `coverage` lists empty, `components: 1` (88,280 cells), `walkable_pct 36.4` = `reachable_pct`.

36.4% is above the 20–35% band, so I held it to the sparse-schematic bar rather than waving it through. Page 2 has **636 drawings — the sparsest onboarded guide in the repo** (659=2404, 660=1506, 24=1468, 658=943). The geometry is arithmetically consistent: aisle pitch 37.9 pt (=3.0 m), shelf runs ~19 pt, corridors ~20 pt, so corridor share ≈ 51% of each aisle block by construction. Cleared with complete probes, not by inspection: all 25 aisle corridors traced green end to end (`AISLE 1–12` north to y=150, `13–25` west to x=100 — the only breaks are the Market back-wall island cases at y 164–186, confirmed `free_raw == False`, i.e. drawn fixtures), and every green blob >6 m from any printed label classified as legitimate open Market/Produce/Bakery-east floor.

### Pass 2 — Visual sweep: no sealed retail floor, no staff floor left green
3×3 crops of `walkable_overlay.png` plus ~12 targeted high-zoom renders with the shipped grid tinted over the PDF. All 30 culled pockets located and classified: 9 staff rooms, 16 checkout-lane interiors, 5 wall cavities ≤10 pt thick. `free_uncut & ~free` is **empty** — zero isolated pockets.

The store-24 failure mode is specifically ruled out. The Pharmacy's sealed room is genuinely staff — its north wall at y≈607 carries two counter/window units (x 152–165, 216–230) and two door swings, and the will-call fixture strip (x 88–147, y 620–636) is walled top and bottom. The pickup corridor y 578–606 and the NW waiting alcove (x 88–136, y 607–620) are green, and the `PHARMACY` anchor's 4.16 m snap lands on the door threshold at (134,620) — the correct customer standing point, not a drawing artifact. I also initially misread the front-left Magazines/Seasonal Items area as white at crop zoom; the high-zoom render settled it as green, and the 432-cell pocket there is a 14 pt wall chase, not retail floor.

Every unanchored printed department was inspected against `geometry.json`: Market, Tortilleria, Meal Simple, Meal Deal, Business Center, Ice ×2, Tobacco, Magazines, Seasonal Items — all have green frontage.

### Pass 3 — Label probes: PASS
I probed all **333** printed words rather than 10. Worst product-label distance to reachable floor: **0.63 m**. Only three words exceed 2 m — `Pharmacy`, `Business`, `Center` — all service-room label centres whose customer frontages are green.

### Pass 5 — Config sanity: PASS
All 10 exclusions and 4 inclusions state a WHY the map supports. Two spot-checks worth recording: the Deli inclusion `[962,578,1040,614]` stops exactly at the service case's top edge, so it does not leak onto the staff side (y>620); and no exclusion covers a shelf label's only frontage — proved by the 333-word probe.

