## Findings (worst first) — 3 found, 3 fixed

**F1 — `walk_truth` must_not at (732,659) was tautological.** *(fix type: walk_truth point)*
`free_raw[732,659]` is already `False` because the restroom **door pictogram artwork** is drawn at (725..739, 654..664). The point is non-free from the drawing alone, so it would keep passing even if the Restrooms room stopped being sealed entirely — the exact "author's blind spot passes its own test" pattern this role exists to catch. Probe: the point is not a member of the 203-cell sealed pocket x[710,758] y[650,674]. **Fixed:** relocated to **(748,658)**, 5 cells deep inside that pocket. Re-audited: zero in-store must_not points are now non-free from artwork alone.

**F2 — six retail sections/departments had no `must` point.** *(fix type: walk_truth point)*
The store-24 failure mode was undefended precisely where the risk is highest:
- **Front-left retail pocket** x 265–385 / y 611–672, holding the `Magazines` and `Seasonal Items` labels — walled off from the Pharmacy by the x 251–265 chase, and the auto `PHARMACY` seal disk is r=130 at (171,657), so a radius change would swallow it silently. → **(285,645)**, **(330,666)**
- **West-wall shelf frontage corridor** x≈112–130, the *only* frontage for five rotated labels (Household Storage and Containers / Paper Towels / Napkins / Bath Tissue / Facial Tissue), sitting directly under the west-wall staff-column exclusion. → **(116,300)**, **(116,520)**
- **Ice ×2 / Tobacco frontages**, each a narrow band between a merchandiser and a sealed front-strip room. → **(505,630)**, **(568,630)**, **(808,628)**
- **Business Center customer frontage**, north of its counter band y 648–655. → **(640,643)**
- **Meat department frontage** (anchor at 868,465; aisles 1–4 were entirely unpinned). → **(859,465)**

**F3 — eleven sealed staff areas / enclosed rooms had no `must_not` point.** *(fix type: walk_truth point)*
Four of the ten exclusion shapes asserted staff status over ~4,000 cells of floor with no test defending the assertion (BOH western extension, second Dairy cooler room, Dairy-walk-in↔Market-back-room gap, west-wall staff column), plus the Seafood staff-door alcove. Six sealed pockets had a pinned twin but were themselves unpinned: second bakery-east room (269 cells, own door at x 1092–1104), second front-strip room behind Tobacco (248, own door at x 582–595), east Restrooms room (196), SE staff-room bank behind the Deli kitchen (127, three door swings), Business Center back-of-counter strip (309), and the Pharmacy/retail chase (244). **Fixed:** 12 points added. Re-audit: every exclusion shape and every sealed pocket ≥100 cells is now covered, except two genuine wall cavities 6 pt and 2 pt thick (behind the cafe counter; along the Dairy walk-in's south wall) — crevices, not rooms.

`walk_truth.json` went from 21/17 to **30 must / 28 must_not**; test count 760 → **780**, all green. Only `data/229/walk_truth.json` was edited — no code, no goldens, no other store (`git diff --stat` is empty; `data/229/` is untracked).

`AUDIT CLEAN — store 229 (3 findings fixed)`
